# std/fs
Read and write files with capability-based security.
Respects AILANG_FS_SANDBOX environment variable for sandboxing.

Requires: FS capability (--caps FS)

## Exports

  readFile(string) -> string ! {FS}
    File reading

  readFileBytes(string) -> Result[string, string] ! {FS}
    Binary file reading as BASE64 TEXT, not bytes: Ok holds a base64 string (use readFileRaw for bytes)

  writeFile(string, string) -> () ! {FS}
    File writing

  writeFileBytes(string, bytes) -> () ! {FS}
    Binary file writing (panics on failure; writeFileBytesResult returns Err instead)

  appendFile(string, string) -> () ! {FS}
    File append (string)

  appendFileBytes(string, bytes) -> () ! {FS}
    Binary file append

  fileExists(string) -> bool ! {FS}
    File existence check

  listDir(string) -> list[string] ! {FS}
    M-DOCPARSE-DX M3: Directory listing

  mkdir(string) -> () ! {FS}
    Create a single directory (parent must exist)

  mkdirAll(string) -> () ! {FS}
    Create a directory and all parent directories (mkdir -p)

  isDir(string) -> bool ! {FS}
    Check if path is a directory

  isFile(string) -> bool ! {FS}
    Check if path is a regular file

  removeFile(string) -> () ! {FS}
    Remove a file or empty directory

  renameFile(string, string) -> () ! {FS}
    Atomically rename (move) a file or directory on the same filesystem (M-FS-RENAME, since v0.35.0)

  readFileResult(string) -> Result[string, string] ! {FS}
    Read file contents as a UTF-8 string, returning Result instead of panicking

  writeFileResult(string, string) -> Result[(), string] ! {FS}
    Write string content to a file, returning Result instead of panicking

  appendFileResult(string, string) -> Result[(), string] ! {FS}
    Append string content to a file, returning Result instead of panicking

  removeFileResult(string) -> Result[(), string] ! {FS}
    Remove a file, returning Result instead of panicking

  mkdirAllResult(string) -> Result[(), string] ! {FS}
    Create directory and all parent directories, returning Result instead of panicking

  mkdirResult(string) -> Result[(), string] ! {FS}
    mkdirResult: Create ONE directory; Err if it already exists (or cannot be created).

  removeDirResult(string) -> Result[(), string] ! {FS}
    removeDirResult: Remove an EMPTY directory (the lock release). Never recursive:

  readFileRaw(string) -> Result[bytes, string] ! {FS}
    Read a file's raw bytes, returning Result instead of panicking (since v0.51.1)

  writeFileBytesResult(string, bytes) -> Result[(), string] ! {FS}
    Write raw bytes to a file (truncates if exists), returning Result instead of panicking (since v0.51.1)

  renameFileResult(string, string) -> Result[(), string] ! {FS}
    Atomically rename (move) a file or directory, returning Result instead of panicking (M-FS-RENAME, since v0.35.0)

  walk(string) -> list[string] ! {FS}
    walk: every regular FILE under root, recursively, sorted (std/string compare).

  glob(string, string) -> list[string] ! {FS}
    glob: walk(root) filtered to paths ending in suffix. Suffix matching only

## Usage

  import std/fs (readFile)
  -- or --
  import std/fs as Fs

